    <statement><p>Suppose that you are climbing a hill whose shape is given by
<m>z = 469 - 0.1 x^2 -0.01 y^2</m>,
and that you are at the point
(40, 30, 300).</p>
<p>In which direction (unit vector) should you proceed initially in order
to reach the top of the hill fastest?</p>
<p><m>\langle</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,<fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>\rangle</m></p>
<p>If you climb in that direction, at what
angle above the horizontal will you be climbing initially (radian
measure)?</p>
<p><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.997199309888456</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
